DESIGN PLAN

STEP 1: DEFINE THE PURPOSE 

The initial step in the development of a solid design plan is to define the purpose of the Web site.
 
STEP 2: IDENTIFY THE AUDIEN

The second step in your design plan is to identify the audience. Although anyone in the world with Internet  access potentially  could be a member of  your Web site’s audience. 

STEP 3: PLAN THE CONTENT 

The design plan is to consider the different types of content you could include in your Web site.
 
STEP 4: PLAN THE STRUCTURE 

With the purpose defined, the audience identified, and the content planned, Step 4 in the development of the design plan is to plan the structure.
 
STEP 5: PLAN THE WEB PAGES 

The Web site's purpose and audience and an understanding of the required content and structure.

STEP 6: PLAN THE NAVIGATION 

The organization, color scheme, and layout determined, the final step in developing a design plan is to plan the navigation system to ensure the success of your Web site. 
